# Notification credentials live here at runtime and are never committed.
#
# Alertmanager reads them through the *_file forms (slack_api_url_file,
# authorization.credentials_file) so that rotating a webhook URL is a file
# write and a SIGHUP rather than a config change in git.
#
# Provision the files here from the secret store (Ansible: monitoring role):
#   slack-api-url            <- Slack incoming webhook for #alerts
#   pagerduty-routing-key    <- PagerDuty Events API v2 integration key
#   oncall-webhook-token     <- bearer token for the internal notification API
*
!.gitignore
